This implementation uses a contiguous array for efficient memory usage and cache locality. The code utilizes `pthread_mutex_t` to ensure thread safety during concurrent access and modification of the array. An integrity verification task runs periodically in its own thread to compute and compare checksums. This approach prioritizes ease of integration with existing systems while managing potential overheads associated with mutex locks.']

